Currently, we have 650K archives collected per day, the size of the {{archive_info.parquet}} gets very big.

As suggested by [~accountid:70121:85182348-77dc-4971-b8a8-a6419cf7776d], we can start by removing some unused columns from the current parquet.
h3. Current columns:
{code:java}
account  inventory_id  system_id  request_id  upload_time  size  file_name
{code}
h3. Columns used by RAT for now:
{code:java}
account  inventory_id  file_name
{code}
h3. Suggested Columns:
{code:java}
account  inventory_id  request_id  date
{code}
 * since the {{file_name}} is a very long string, we can generate it based on the {{request_id}} and {{date}} to shrink the size further.

items.toString:
The following is the concern raised by Lloyd,

 
Something to check If you have not already figured out the Rat-2 hanging issue. Since aggregate checks self.gather_done >= self.num_gathers, to determine if all gathers are done, it may be resetting the counter if the aggregate component restarts. For instance let's say aggregate has already received one "done" message from aggregate and increments the counter and then for some reason gets restarted, in this case the counter gets reset to zero. Now that check will never be true sinc the previously increment counter was reset.
It seems like I noticed while job 262 was still running last week that it had restarted at least one time, I may not be remembering correctly. I also noticed that even though both gathers sent a done message to aggregate (according to the gather log) the aggregate log does contain the message "{color:#000000}Shutting down rat-aggregate for Job ID \{self.job_id}" (line 496), which it would get if self.gathers_done was greater than self.num_gathers.{color}
{color:#000000}In this case aggregate would never try to shut down the workers, gathers and aggregate.{color}

